# REI orchestration (canonical routing)

## Default (mandatory unless opted out)

- **REI orchestration is the default for all substantive work.** The parent agent **routes** via **Task** to **🏠(REI)** subagents; it does **not** implement product changes unless the user **explicitly** opts out for the **current** request (see [Explicit opt-out](#explicit-opt-out)).
- Single source of truth for routing, opt-out, continue/resume, and multitask delegation. Other files **cross-reference** here—not duplicate playbooks.

## What counts as substantive work

Route through REI when the request involves: new features, behavior changes, refactors, bug fixes, multi-file/multi-repo edits, migrations, config that changes runtime behavior, executing plans under `plans/`, or slash commands that launch work (`/plan-feature`, `/fix-bug`, `/implement-plan`, etc.) unless the command says otherwise.

**Task not required:** short answers, read-only navigation, explaining behavior, status checks, questions with **no** code change.

## Default implementation chain

1. **🏠(REI) Planner** (Task) → plan under `plans/features/` or `plans/bugs/` (`.cursor/skills/plan-feature/SKILL.md`).
2. **User approves** the plan—or **explicitly** waives planning/approval (see opt-out).
3. **🏠(REI) Implementer** (Task) → `.cursor/skills/execute-plan/SKILL.md` (branch-gate, Test-engineer → Reviewer per `.cursor/agents/implementer.md`).

**Exact Task `subagent_type` values:**

| Role | `subagent_type` |
|------|-----------------|
| Planner | `🏠(REI) Planner` |
| Implementer | `🏠(REI)  Implementer` |
| Researcher | `🏠(REI) Researcher` |
| Test-engineer | `🏠(REI) Test-engineer` |
| Reviewer | `🏠(REI) Reviewer` |

(Implementer has **two spaces** after `REI)`.)

## Planner before implementation

Parent chat must **not** patch features/bugs unless: (1) approved plan + **Task → Implementer**, (2) **explicit opt-out**, or (3) trivial non-behavioral typo/comment the user pointed to. If unclear, **ask once**.

## Continue / resume (not an opt-out)

"continue", "go ahead", "approved", "implement it", etc. do **not** waive REI or allow parent patching.

- Plan **approved** (or waiver): **Task → Implementer** with plan path—do not implement in parent chat.
- Plan exists, **not** approved: blocked transition per `.cursor/docs/step-transition-contract.md`; wait for explicit approval/waiver.
- No plan, substantive work: **Task → Planner** first (unless planning waived).

## Step transitions

At significant boundaries, enforce `.cursor/docs/step-transition-contract.md` (`Status`, `Reason`, `Next required action` with concrete options; approval gates require exact approve/waiver replies).

## Post-`/design-product` auto-routing

After **🏠(REI) product-designer**: **Task → Implementer** only if implementation-ready (scope locked, boundaries clear, contracts/edge cases/validation/sequence explicit); else **Task → Planner**; if ambiguous, default Planner. Explicit opt-out still applies.

## Multitask / Task tool

- Background runs use named REI subagents for substantive work.
- Do **not** default to `resume: "self"` for features/bugs—that bypasses Implementer branch-gate/handoffs.
- `resume: "self"` only when user explicitly requested self-fork **and** opted out of Implementer.
- `run_in_background` on **Task → Implementer** (or Planner), not nameless self-fork, unless opted out.

## Explicit opt-out

User must **clearly** opt out for the **current** request:

| Intent | Example phrases |
|--------|-----------------|
| No subagents | "main chat only", "no subagents", "skip Task" |
| Parent implements | "implement in this chat", "inline fix" |
| Skip formal planning | "waive formal planning", "skip the plan" |
| Skip plan approval | "waive plan approval", "implement immediately" (when clear) |
| Q&A only | "just explain", "read only", "don't change code" |

**Not opt-out:** "please fix", "fix the bug", "continue", "ok", "go" alone.

## `/fix-bug`

Follow `.cursor/commands/fix-bug.md`: Planner → separate approval → Implementer → test/review.

## Parent vs Implementer

Default conversation agent **delegates** to **Implementer** via Task; no production patches for substantive work except opt-out or trivial non-behavioral edit.

## Required inputs

Ask concise clarifying questions when required inputs are missing. Stage security gates: `.cursor/docs/security-gates.md`.

## Agency Agents (optional specialists)

When `.cursor/agents/` includes Agency slugs (e.g. `backend-architect`), use them for **domain expertise** only—never as a replacement for Planner / Implementer / Test-engineer / Reviewer.

- Map and invocation: `.cursor/skills/agency-integration/SKILL.md`
- Discovery: `/agency` or `.cursor/catalog/`
- Thin always-on reminder: `.cursor/rules/agency-integration.mdc`
